-- ============================================================================
-- PD1 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Nodal Analysis & Well Performance, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE INFLOW. What the reservoir will give, at what
-- pressure, and how confidently. It ends before the tubing is mentioned,
-- because half of a nodal answer is a statement about the rock alone.
--
-- THE THREE FAMILIES AGREE ABOVE THE BUBBLE POINT AND SEPARATE BELOW IT, and
-- that is the whole shape of the tier. A straight line is exactly the
-- composite relation while the flowing pressure stays above the bubble point.
-- Below it the line keeps extrapolating a constant productivity index into a
-- fluid that has started to release gas, and the three answers walk apart.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A productivity index is calibrated from ONE
-- test, and the test position decides which index you get. On the capstone
-- well the true index is 1.856946 stb/d/psi and a straight line fitted to the
-- same two phase test backs out 1.818182, an error of -0.038765 stb/d/psi that
-- no amount of care in the arithmetic can recover. The test was taken below
-- the bubble point, so the line is being asked a question it cannot answer,
-- and it answers anyway. Reading the calibration back at the test point
-- reproduces the test exactly in all three families, which is why calibration
-- agreement proves nothing.
--
-- THE RECORDED ENGINE DEFECT THIS TIER OWNS. `gasPwfAtRate` reads a SAMPLED
-- gas inflow curve by linear interpolation, and the sampling is even in
-- PRESSURE, so it is sparse in RATE exactly where the curve is steepest. The
-- error is one to three psi through the body of both empirical families and
-- reaches thirteen psi at the low rate end of a strongly turbulent one. The
-- sign never changes: the chord always reads low. This is the reason the
-- inverse reading is done by a root find rather than by reading a chord off a
-- table, and the reason the forward and inverse readings are two different
-- operations rather than one operation run backwards.
--
-- ABSOLUTE OPEN FLOW IS AN INDEX, NOT A PLAN. It is the forward reading at
-- zero flowing pressure, a boundary that no well is ever produced at, and the
-- engine will report one for a well whose node has no solution at all. The
-- capstone's open flow is 3848.0055 stb/d and its stable operating window is
-- 24.6453 stb/d wide, 0.64 percent of it, which is the sharpest statement in
-- the course of what an open flow does and does not tell you.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the inflow
-- relation itself and the reservoir pressure it was built at.
-- ============================================================================

values ('nodal', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-well-can-deliver","title":"What a Well Can Deliver","lesson_keys":["l01-two-halves-of-one-question","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-pressure-is-the-currency"]},{"key":"m02-the-straight-line","title":"The Straight Line","lesson_keys":["l01-productivity-index","l02-when-a-line-is-honest","l03-calibrating-from-one-test","l04-drawdown","l05-where-the-line-breaks"]},{"key":"m03-below-the-bubble-point","title":"Below the Bubble Point","lesson_keys":["l01-why-the-curve-bends","l02-vogel","l03-the-composite-ipr","l04-the-join-at-the-bubble-point","l05-choosing-a-model"]},{"key":"m04-reading-the-curve-both-ways","title":"Reading the Curve Both Ways","lesson_keys":["l01-rate-from-a-pressure","l02-pressure-from-a-rate","l03-why-the-inverse-needs-a-root-find","l04-sampling-and-what-it-costs","l05-what-a-reading-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m05-absolute-open-flow","title":"Absolute Open Flow","lesson_keys":["l01-what-aof-is","l02-what-aof-is-not","l03-comparing-wells-with-it","l04-the-numbers-that-travel"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
